<title>USA: U.S. Sept personal income rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept personal income rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   Sept   Aug-Rev from  Jul-Rev from  June</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.6    0.5    0.6    0.1    0.1    0.9</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.6    0.5    0.5    0.1    0.1    0.8</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.4    0.4    0.5   -0.1   -0.1    0.7</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.1    0.5    0.6    0.2    0.2   -0.5</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs     -0.1    0.5    0.5   Unch   Unch   -0.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Sept  Aug-Rev from  Jul-Rev from   June</p>
<p> Income		   6,542  6,501  6,502  6,465  6,466  6,460</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,661  5,627  5,631  5,601  5,603  5,597</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,339  5,335  5,338  5,309  5,308  5,298</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,175  5,172  5,174  5,145  5,145  5,136</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   634    643    644    624    625    632</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,547  1,540  1,544  1,544  1,543  1,541</p>
<p> -Services		2,994  2,988  2,986  2,977  2,977  2,963</p>
<p> Personal Saving	  323    292    293    292    295    299</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.7    5.2    5.2    5.2    5.3    5.3</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Sept  Aug-Rev from  Jul-Rev from   June</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,696  3,665  3,667  3,636  3,637  3,643</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   680    680    683    675    676    675</p>
<p> -Services		1,289  1,272  1,273  1,260  1,260  1,263</p>
<p> -Government		647    645    645    643    643    640</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    524    521    520    521    520    519</p>
<p> -Farm			 48     49     45     49     47     48</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  476    472    474    472    473    471</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected September personal income to rise by 0.6 percent and spending to be up 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The 5.7 percent personal savings rate in September was the highest since December 1993, when it stood at 6.3 percent, the department said.</p>
